 * HISTORY
 * $Log: vs.defs,v $
 * Revision 1.20  1995/02/01  23:20:18  bolsen
 *  Reviewer(s): Jerry Toman
 *  Risk: Medium (lots of files)
 *  Module(s): Too many to list
 *  Configurations built: STD, LITE, & RAMDISK
 *
 *  Added or Updated the Locus Copyright message.
 *
 * Revision 1.19  1994/12/22  02:15:17  nina
 *  Reviewer:hobbes
 *  Risk:Medium
 *  Benefit or PTS #:10356
 *  Testing:Test case and TCP/IP EATS in various network configs
 *  Module(s):
 *
 * 	net/rtsock.c
 * 	netinet/in_proto.c
 * 	vsocket/vs_chouse.h
 * 	vsocket/vs_chouse.c
 * 	vsocket/vs.defs
 * 	vsocket/vs_ipc.c
 * 	vsocket/vs_subr.c
 * 	vsocket/vs_netops.c
 *
 *   The was only seen in systems with multiple network configurations
 *   when a user attempted to bind to INADDR_ANY/port 0. In this
 *   situation, the system is supposed to pick the port number for
 *   the caller. The problem occurred because the VSOCKET code
 *   didn't ensure that the primary socket and each secondary socket used
 *   the same port number.
 *
 *   Now, a bind to port 0 results in an RPC to the clearinghouse to
 *   pick a port number, based on the domain and protocol of the socket.
 *
 * Revision 1.18  1994/11/18  20:52:00  mtm
 * Copyright additions/changes
 *
 * Revision 1.17  1994/07/28  22:16:53  yazz
 *  Reviewer: Mike Leibensperger
 *  Risk: Lo
 *  Benefit or PTS #: 10421
 *  Testing: EATs tcp-ip
 *  Module(s): server/vsocket/vs.defs, .../vs_subr.c, .../vs_ipc.c,
 *             .../vsocket.h
 * Unused simpleroutine r_vs_fp_unref_svr() removed.
 *
 * Revision 1.16  1994/05/04  22:13:52  mjl
 * Merge revision 1.15.2.1 from R1_2 branch into main trunk.
 *
 *  Reviewer:
 *  Risk:
 *  Benefit or PTS #:
 *  Testing:
 *  Module(s):
 *
 * Revision 1.15.2.1  1994/04/27  23:03:22  yazz
 *  Reviewer: Charlie Johnson, Bob Yasi
 *  Risk: Medium
 *  Benefit or PTS #: #7537 + select rewrite
 *  Testing: VSX, EATS, bobtest, Eval
 *  Module(s):
 * 	server/bsd/subr_select.c
 * 	server/sys/select.h
 * 	server/sys/socketvar.h
 * 	server/sys/user.h
 * 	server/tnc/un_debug.c
 * 	server/tnc/un_debug.h
 * 	server/uxkern/bsd_2.defs
 * 	server/uxkern/bsd_server_side.c
 * 	server/uxkern/fsvr.defs
 * 	server/uxkern/fsvr2_server_side.c
 * 	server/uxkern/fsvr_port.c
 * 	server/uxkern/fsvr_subr.c
 * 	server/uxkern/port_hash.c
 * 	server/uxkern/port_hash.h
 * 	server/vsocket/mi_config.c
 * 	server/vsocket/sys_vsocket.c
 * 	server/vsocket/two_way_hash.h
 * 	server/vsocket/vs.defs
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_chouse.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_debug.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_init.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_ipc.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_netops.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_subr.c
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_subr.h
 * 	server/vsocket/vs_types.h
 * 	server/vsocket/vsocket.h
 * TNC select rewrite.
 *  - For r_vs_socreate(): all networking vsockets get S+R rights, so OUT
 *     socket_port arg in r_vs_socreate() can use default COPY_SEND semantics.
 *     Also add socket_addr OUT arg, stored in rvs to ease debugging.
 *  - For r_vs_sodequeue(): use COPY_SEND for OUT sock_port.
 *  - Combine r_vs_getstate_immed() and r_vs_select_dequeue() since they
 *     were always called one after the other.
 *  - For rvs_select_enqueue() and r_vs_select_dequeue: use integer select id
 *     to identify the select call when enqueueing/dequeueing remotely.
 *     Use MOVE_SEND so that remote queue entry really holds the file
 *     svrref send right, and on error return the right as an OUT arg.
 *  - Add r_vs_scrub_remote_selects() -- when select_wakeup() discovers a
 *     dead drp, this ensures that a cleanup FOP_SELECT is done in all cases.
 *  - The r_vs_fp_unref_svr() RPC is never used and is checked in "just in case".
 *
 * Revision 1.15  1993/09/20  23:58:31  cfj
 * Merge R1.1 bug fixes into main stem.
 *
 * Revision 1.14.2.1  1993/09/20  23:49:32  cfj
 * Bug fix for PTS #6663.  The correct netserver is now chosen.
 *
 * Revision 1.14  1993/09/01  01:40:30  bolsen
 * 08-31-93 Locus code drop for multiple netservers.
 *
 * Revision 1.13  1993/07/29  21:55:17  cfj
 * 07-29-93 Locus code drop to fix select() and multiple network server
 * slowdown.
 *
 * Revision 1.12  1993/07/14  18:48:45  cfj
 * OSF/1 AD 1.0.4 code drop from Locus.
 *
 * Revision 1.1.1.6  1993/07/01  21:13:28  cfj
 * Adding new code from vendor
 *
 * Revision 1.11  1993/05/20  16:04:28  cfj
 * Merge of 05-18-93 code drop from Locus.
 *
 * Revision 3.27  93/08/26  11:02:18  mjl
 * [LCCbug #0374; #0376 no longer reproducible; maybe fixes #0372]
 * Replace r_vs_ioctl() RPC's fixed length INOUT array argument with
 * two variable length array arguments, one IN and one OUT.  Prevents
 * server addressing exceptions that occured when all N bytes of fixed
 * arg weren't allocated in server's address space.
 * 
 * Revision 3.26  93/08/17  19:29:14  mjl
 * Add "out" return value for r_vs_socreate().  Add "in" client_node
 * argument for if_list().
 * 
 * Revision 3.25  93/08/16  18:56:23  bhk
 * Removed remote sleep routines. [# 346]
 * split remote getstate into synchronouse and asynchronous calls [#346]
 * Added creds port to close to avoid crash[ #347]
 * 
 * Revision 3.24  93/08/11  09:06:22  bhk
 * Changed soreadable to be a simpleroutine to avoid banging on the remote
 * network server for read requests
 * 
 * Revision 3.23  93/08/09  18:56:11  bhk
 * Passed the target port over as a port name in r_m_vs_sosleep to
 * allow the primary virtual socket to identify the secondary which
 * woke up.  Removed the parent port from r_m_vs_sosleep and used the
 * cached callback port.  fixes bug 323
 * 
 * Revision 3.22  93/08/09  15:52:45  bhk
 * added callback port to remote socket creation
 * 
 * Revision 3.21  93/08/06  17:56:35  bhk
 * removed transid from multiple sleeps
 * added lock to remote soreadable
 * 
 * Revision 3.20  93/07/28  15:02:56  bhk
 * Added ipc to remotely unlock a socket.
 * 
 * Revision 3.19  93/05/10  14:42:52  bhk
 * Syncronized state after connection request
 * 
 * Revision 3.18  93/05/07  15:22:07  nina
 * Extended the interface of if_list to return an array
 * of mach ports.  Extended the interface of 
 * if_get_nearest_server() to return the node number
 * of the selected network server.
 * 
 * Revision 3.17  93/05/05  22:34:43  mjl
 * New clearinghouse check-in RPCs for MIv3.  Name all clearinghouse RPCs
 * consistently (i.e. "if_*").
 * 
 * Revision 3.16  93/04/12  15:52:33  nina
 * Added two RPCs to support single system semantics for
 * SIOCGIFCONF, SIOCADDRT and SIOCDELRT
 * 
 * Revision 3.15  93/04/03  11:53:07  klh
 * Split select into three parts (check, enqueue, dequeue). (klh for bhk)
 * 
 * Revision 3.14  93/03/19  17:31:13  bhk
 * added the select dequeue call, removed the scanning parameter from
 * vs_select and changed the lock parameter in getstate from a boolean to
 * an int
 * 
 * Revision 3.13  93/02/10  21:07:56  klh
 * Additional checkin to sync up RCS comments
 * 
 * Revision 3.12  93/02/09  18:14:41  mjl
 * Henceforth, thou shalt pass thy address families as integers!
 * 
 * Revision 3.12  93/02/08  16:53:37  bhk
 * fixed definition for r_vs_select no to make a sendright but to copy one
 * 
 * Revision 3.11  93/01/11  19:16:45  bhk
 * passed the socket family separately in if_lookup to allow
 * passing a NULL address.
 * 
 * Revision 3.10  93/01/04  20:41:51  bhk
 * Added transaction ID to remote vsocket calls to allow signals to
 * be processed correctly
 * 
 * Revision 3.9  92/10/27  17:51:47  bhk
 * replaced pruaddr (the old usrreq virtual operation) with getaddr
 * (the new virtual operation)
 * 
 * Revision 3.8  92/10/07  16:16:33  bhk
 * added not parameter to if_lookup to allow the return of
 * MACH_PORT_NULL as a server port which represents the
 * local network server.
 * 
 * Revision 3.7  92/09/24  17:10:11  bhk
 * fixed select timeout problem, added not to interface regististation with
 * the clearinghouse
 * 
 * Revision 3.6  92/07/26  17:49:26  bhk
 * addes support for select and getpeername
 * 
 * Revision 3.5  92/06/26  14:05:39  chrisp
 * Change sockaddr_t to sockarg_t so that MIG understands it's a variable
 * 	length character array for the 860.
 * 
 * Revision 3.4  92/06/16  18:44:58  bhk
 * added return values remote sleep/wakeup and shutdown routines
 * 
 * Revision 3.3  92/05/06  16:11:13  bhk
 * added VSOP_SLEEP inet ipc calls
 * fixed send_long to return amount of data written
 * 
 * Revision 3.2  92/04/22  17:06:55  bhk
 * added getsockname mig definition.
 * 
 * Revision 3.1  92/04/20  21:52:28  klh
 * 	Fix RCS comments
 * 
 * Revision 3.0  92/04/20  17:21:31  bhk
 * Genesis  Remote Virtual Socket RPC definitions
 *
 * $EndLog$
